Testing Project: Selenium WebDriver with TestNG

* Build the project using Selenium WebDriver and TestNG.
* Use `dependsOnMethods` and `priority` annotations to make tests dependent on each other where necessary.
* Use `@Parameters`.
* Make your test classes executable via an XML file.

---

# Test Case 1: Registration Test

* Navigate to:

  `https://demo.nopcommerce.com/register?returnUrl=%2F`

* Click the **Register** link.

* Enter **First Name** and **Last Name**.

* Select the **Date of Birth** using dropdown menus.

* Enter an **Email** address.

* Enter **Password** and **Confirm Password**.

* Click the **Register** button.

* Verify that registration is completed successfully.

---

# Test Case 2: Login Test

* Click the **Login** button.
* Enter the registered **Email** and **Password**.
* Click the **LOG IN** button.
* Verify that login is completed successfully.

---

# Test Case 3: Data Provider Login Test

* Click the **Login** button.
* Retrieve valid and invalid **Email** and **Password** combinations from a Data Provider method.
* Click the **LOG IN** button.
* Verify whether login is successful or unsuccessful accordingly.

---

# Test Case 4: Tab Menu Test

* Store the names of the products displayed in the tab menu in a list.
* Locate the tab menu list elements.
* Verify that the located list elements contain the expected tab menu product names.

---

# Test Case 5: Order Gifts Test

* Click **Gifts** from the tab menu.
* Randomly select one of the physical gift products.
* On the product page, fill in:

  * **Recipient Name**
  * **Sender Name**
  * **Message**
* Click **ADD TO CART**.
* Verify that the product is added to the cart successfully.

---

# Test Case 6: Order Computer Test

* Hover over **Computers** in the tab menu.
* Click **Desktops** from the dropdown menu.
* On the opened page, select **Build your own computer**.
* Randomly select a **RAM** option.
* Randomly select an **HDD** option.
* Click **ADD TO CART**.
* Verify that the product is added to the cart successfully.

---

# Test Case 7: Parameterized Search Test

* Enter **"Adobe Photoshop CS4"** into the search box using a parameter retrieved from the XML file.
* Click the **Search** button.
* Verify that the product title on the results page contains the searched text.

